  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 AM MDT Mon Jun 22 2026\n\nUpper high centered over the Big Bend region and the Chihuahuan \nDesert of northern Mexico. On the southern margin, a couple of \neasterly waves move across central Mexico with no appreciable \nimpact on our area. To the north of the center are some higher \nclouds moving east across the northern CWA. Very warm 500mb temps \nof -1C to -3C, so capping of the airmass continues. \n\nThe upper high does become more circular by Tuesday and \nespecially Wednesday, allowing some sub-tropical moisture to move \nback into the area. 500mb temps also cool, turning our airmass \nback to slightly unstable. Thus slight chances of thunderstorms \nreturn to the area Wednesday, mostly over the mountains. The \nslight chance will continue Thursday and Friday and POPs extend \ndown into the lowlands. Hot weather will continue, with Tue/Wed \nbeing the hottest days. Heat Advisories out through Wednesday and \nmay be needed beyond. \n\nSaturday and Sunday...high center drifts south and west as \nPacific trough cuts through the central Rockies. This increases \nour west flow which scours out any moisture still left, and it \ninduces breezy afternoons each day. Unless the mountains get some \nsignificant rain, our airmass and fuels are going to go through a \nlong stretch of drying out. Thus with the afternoon winds, fire \nconditions will approach critical and possibly Red Flag \nconditions. Stay tuned.",
